Waaah!

I made it the second time. I got the amulet and went as fast as possible
to the first floor. The stupid wizard attacked me several times, but no
problem. As I reached the exit the wizard came again, summoned some of 
his evil creatures including a cockatrice. The ring of conflict did good
work, several monster turned to stone. Then the misery began:

I wielded the pick-axe and tried to smash some of the statues.
THE PICK-AXE WAS CURSED !!!  No holy water, no remove curse spell/scroll,
no potion of water, no scroll of enchant weapon, no chance for praying.
*nothing*  No chance to wield my blessed +5 Stormbringer ... 
At this point, I thought it was all over.
So I went up to the endgame ....

The wizard attacked again and summoned several creatures. Through the
ring of conflict I was able to concentrate on the wizard. (imagine this:
with a pick-axe !!!). I brought him down to 50 hp as he teleported away
to heal himself. 

I started running like mad and tried to make my way to the altar.
The rooms filled with dragons, liches etc etc were no problem. On my way
to the altar the wizard attacked four times ...
 
But: I DID IT ! yeah yeah yeah. I won the endgame with a cursed pick-axe.

Ah yes: I had an AC of -22, shield of reflection, helm of telepathy,
gray dragon scale mail, speed boots, gloves of dexterity, 202 hp, 3 
amulets of life saving (I only need one, 'cause I choked over food :-),
+5 Stormbringer, crysknife, +3 Excalibur, all weapons and armor were 
rust-proofed cause I found several magic markers. Later on I wished for
a wand of polymorph, but except for an polished silver shield I only got
rubbish.

Ok, don't flame me. I will never wield equipment again after I met the wizard. 
